From: Yealink T48S open firmware <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: bcm: add the BCMRING family (BCM11107, BCM11188), device tree only

Mainline dropped mach-bcmring in 3.7. Bring the family back as a device
tree only platform: no board file, only the Kconfig entry that selects the
drivers the SoC needs (PL192 interrupt controllers, SP804 timers, AMBA
peripherals). Everything else comes from the device tree.

---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-bcm/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-bcm/Kconfig
@@ -6,6 +6,23 @@ menuconfig ARCH_BCM
 
 if ARCH_BCM
 
+comment "BCMRING SoCs"
+
+config ARCH_BCMRING
+	bool "Broadcom BCMRING SoCs (BCM11107 family, BCM11188)"
+	depends on ARCH_MULTI_V6
+	select ARM_AMBA
+	select ARM_VIC
+	select ARM_TIMER_SP804
+	select GPIOLIB
+	help
+	  Broadcom's BCM11107 family of VoIP SoCs (ARM1176JZF-S), as found
+	  in the BCM11188 of the Yealink SIP-T48S desk phone. Device tree
+	  only: PL192 interrupt controllers, SP804 timers, PL011 UARTs.
+	  The boot loader is expected to have set up the PLLs, the pin
+	  functions and the memory controller; the clocks are described
+	  as fixed in the device tree.
+
 comment "IPROC architected SoCs"
 
 config ARCH_BCM_IPROC
